From afa612d2f30609a4c68063c005c7d10b0b30dd87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 19:25:05 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ui): router machine kind shows the router options on the
 Milling tab

A machine file can state the kind "router". It reads as a mill in every
rule, and machine::is_router reads it as a router. The new
router_offer::router_options lists what the setup's machine offers. The
Sheet job group, the corner relief rows and the MCP get_job field
setups[].router_options read that list. A mill offers none; a stated
option stays shown. The six shipped router files now state "router".

Fixes #2410

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
